  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene of reverence",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual scene of the person kneeling in prayer before a light source, as this scene is used metaphorically to represent the reverence and gratitude owed to bomb disposal experts. The text 'thank you for service' reinforces this projection by inviting the user to acknowledge and honor the service of these individuals, positioning the viewer as someone who should feel gratitude or respect for their sacrifice. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me' in the text, but the overall framing of the meme (visual and textual) creates an implicit projection where the user is expected to identify with the act of gratitude and reverence depicted.",
